# Download Apache DataFu

Apache DataFu is released as source code.  The source releases are available for download from the [Apache Software Foundation](http://www.apache.org/dyn/closer.cgi/datafu/).

## Latest Release

The latest release is [Apache DataFu 2.1.0](http://www.apache.org/dyn/closer.cgi/datafu/datafu-2.1.0/).

## Verification

It is essential that you verify the integrity of the downloaded files using the PGP or SHA signatures.  Please read the [Verifying Apache HTTP Server Releases](http://www.apache.org/info/verification.html) page for more information on why you should verify our releases.

The PGP signatures can be verified using PGP or GPG.  First download the [KEYS](http://www.apache.org/dist/datafu/KEYS) file as well as the asc signature file for the particular distribution.  It is recommended that you get these files from the main distribution directory and not from the mirrors.

    gpg --import KEYS

or

    gpg --import <(curl http://www.apache.org/dist/datafu/KEYS)

To verify the binaries/sources you can download the relevant asc files for it from main distribution directory and follow the below guide.

    gpg --verify apache-datafu-sources-x.y.z.tgz.asc

The command above will assume you are verifying `apache-datafu-sources-x.y.z.tgz` and produce "Good signature" if the archive is valid.

## Source Release

### Prerequisites

Make sure you have [Gradle](http://gradle.org/gradle-download/) installed.  Extract the source and generate the `gradlew` script that's used for building.  The `gradlew` script uses the specific version of Gradle that DataFu is intended to be built with.

    tar xvf apache-datafu-sources-<%= current_page.data.version %>.tgz
    cd apache-datafu-sources-<%= current_page.data.version %>
    gradle wrapper --gradle-version 9.1.0

To build the JARs, run:

    ./gradlew assemble

This will produce JARs in the following directories:

* `datafu-pig/build/libs/`
* `datafu-hourglass/build/libs/`
* `datafu-spark/build/libs/`

## Building from Git

If you want to build from the latest source code, you can clone the repository:

    git clone https://git-wip-us.apache.org/repos/asf/datafu.git
    cd datafu
    ./gradlew assemble

## Previous Releases

All previous releases of Apache DataFu are available from the [Apache archive](http://archive.apache.org/dist/datafu/).

## Release Notes

For information about what's new in each release, see the [release notes](http://datafu.apache.org/docs/datafu/release-notes.html).

## Maven Central

Apache DataFu artifacts are also available from [Maven Central](http://search.maven.org/#search%7Cgav%7C1%7Cg%3A%22org.apache.datafu%22).

### Maven Coordinates

#### DataFu Pig
```xml
<dependency>
  <groupId>org.apache.datafu</groupId>
  <artifactId>datafu-pig</artifactId>
  <version>2.1.0</version>
</dependency>
```

#### DataFu Hourglass
```xml
<dependency>
  <groupId>org.apache.datafu</groupId>
  <artifactId>datafu-hourglass</artifactId>
  <version>2.1.0</version>
</dependency>
```

#### DataFu Spark
```xml
<dependency>
  <groupId>org.apache.datafu</groupId>
  <artifactId>datafu-spark_2.11</artifactId>
  <version>2.1.0</version>
</dependency>
```

or for Scala 2.12:

```xml
<dependency>
  <groupId>org.apache.datafu</groupId>
  <artifactId>datafu-spark_2.12</artifactId>
  <version>2.1.0</version>
</dependency>
```

### Gradle Coordinates

#### DataFu Pig
```gradle
compile 'org.apache.datafu:datafu-pig:2.1.0'
```

#### DataFu Hourglass
```gradle
compile 'org.apache.datafu:datafu-hourglass:2.1.0'
```

#### DataFu Spark
```gradle
compile 'org.apache.datafu:datafu-spark_2.11:2.1.0'
```

or for Scala 2.12:

```gradle
compile 'org.apache.datafu:datafu-spark_2.12:2.1.0'
```

## Support

If you encounter any issues with the downloads or have questions about Apache DataFu, please:

1. Check the [documentation](http://datafu.apache.org/docs/)
2. Search the [mailing list archives](http://mail-archives.apache.org/mod_mbox/datafu-user/)
3. Join the [user mailing list](mailto:user-subscribe@datafu.apache.org)
4. Report issues on [JIRA](https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/DATAFU)